 [38;5;248mNo goal tool needed? The objective says use no ordinary tools and do not access files. The [39;38;5;48mgoal[39;38;5;248;38;5;248m tool is for goal-mode management, not an "ordinary tool". Should I call goal complete? The instructions say before goal complete, audit repo state... but here deliverable is the PM_RESULT line itself, verifiable from admitted context without tools. The task is deterministic JSON assembly; completion evidence is the output line itself. Calling goal({op:"complete"}) after emitting the result seems     [0m
[0m[K [38;5;248mappropriate for goal mode. But the constraint "Use no ordinary tools" refers to file/bash tools; goal tool is meta. However, calling goal complete would require me to emit a tool call and then continue. The final nonempty line must be exactly one PM_RESULT line. If I call the goal tool, tool calls come before the final answer. Hmm, but the format guide says emit stop sequence after writing the call, then halt — meaning a turn with a tool call ends. Then next turn I'd give the answer.[39m           [0m
